WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.970
Hold a strong magnet near an iron nail.

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:04.880
The nail leaps to it.

3
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.210
Now hold it near a copper pipe.

4
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.000
Nothing seems to happen.

5
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:13.290
Stranger still: a single
charge, sitting perfectly still,

6
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.880
makes no magnetic field at all.

7
00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:19.290
And no one has ever found
a north pole on its own.

8
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.290
So what is different inside the iron?

9
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:26.560
In this mission, you'll find out
where magnetism really comes from.

10
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.600
Then you'll sort materials
into three families,

11
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:33.860
by how strongly, and which
way, they respond to a magnet.

12
00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:37.800
Your mission: explain what
is different inside the iron.
